+# Candidate C: finite rectilinear subdivision of actual leaf domains
+
+This is an independent candidate against commit `04d889f911ba6c89981752df02cc2ad7a67ddc0f`.
+It constructs missing sheets; it does not infer completeness from a manifold check or residual samples.
+The production fallback runs only when an existing prepared octree leaf has exhausted its refinement criteria.
+Successful ordinary fast exports retain their existing mesh path. Later mesher-only failures still use existing recovery.
+
+## Exact mathematical domain
+
+The accepted expression is a nonempty hard min/max tree of signed boxes. Every original occurrence is retained,
+including its ordered path through the tree. Actual transforms must be identity, dimensions finite and positive,
+and both represented endpoints `pos-half` and `pos+half` must equal the corresponding exact dyadic sums.
+Every primitive's endpoints must lie strictly inside the lattice root domain. This deliberately excludes harmless
+large cutters as well as unbounded complements when the bounded construction cannot establish its premises.
+
+The scalar zero set is the continuous real box/min/max field with these actual represented coefficients.
+It is not the discontinuous machine-arithmetic map obtained by rounding an arbitrary real query point.
+The existing scalar evaluator is retained for output residual checking; this module does not add a general scene evaluator.
+
+Cell domains are **actual rounded `cell_aabb` boxes**. Their endpoints must equal the canonical `point_to_world`
+map at the same integer lattice keys. This is not a claim that either computation equals an exact nominal affine map.
+The lattice is validated before shifts or maps: depth 1–14, consistent resolution/span/step, finite origins and positive
+finite size/step. Cell indices and keys must agree, and no two supplied leaves may overlap in their interiors.
+
+All original box boundary planes and all represented leaf boundary coordinates are inserted into one sorted coordinate
+set per axis. Signed zero denotes one coordinate. Cartesian cells are defined by exact coordinate ranks. A coordinate
+is either one event or an **open interval** between adjacent events; no rounded midpoint is required.
+
+## Complete classification, including zero-only pieces
+
+For a box, the sign on an open stratum is constant because its boundary planes belong to the coordinate arrangement.
+The implementation determines that sign by comparing interval endpoints with the exact box endpoints. A fixed coordinate
+on a face gives zero only if the other coordinates stay inside the box. Negation reverses signs.
+
+The identities
+
+`sign(min(a,b)) = min(sign(a),sign(b))` and `sign(max(a,b)) = max(sign(a),sign(b))`
+
+hold with the ordered signs `-1 < 0 < +1`. Folding the **original expression tree** therefore gives the complete sign
+of every open 0D, 1D, 2D and 3D stratum. A single postorder pass also retains every tied original zero occurrence:
+a subtree whose result is nonzero truncates its accumulated zero owners. No algebraic simplification, advisory ID,
+proximity tolerance or geometry deduplication replaces the original occurrences.
+
+Every zero stratum must have both positive and negative incident open 3D regions. This rejects zero-only sheets, lines,
+points and shells such as `A-A`; these cannot silently disappear because an occupancy-only boundary is empty.
+The final indexed link test rejects contacts where both signs exist but the boundary is nonmanifold.
+The resulting construction accepts only closed orientable 2-manifold surfaces, possibly with multiple components or genus.
+
+## Construction and shared cell boundaries
+
+Every zero open 2D rectangle with opposite signs on its two sides is emitted with its negative-to-positive orientation.
+Its four grid keys define two triangles. Thus every exposed rectangle appears exactly once, and only exposed rectangles
+appear. This enumerates enclosed components, annular patches, hollow walls and several disjoint sheets in a cell without
+requiring any pre-existing boundary loop.
+
+A rectangle must lie in the closure of at least one actual retained leaf. Otherwise construction fails with `missing_cell`.
+The global cuts guarantee that an open rectangle cannot partially overlap a leaf: each coordinate boundary is a cut.
+If the surface itself lies on a shared cell face, both closed cell incidences are recorded. Exactly one leaf owns emission,
+selected by ordered geometric leaf ID. This is a half-open emission convention; it does not delete the other cell's closed
+target. At a coarse/fine face the same global cuts restrict to identical rectangles and edge subdivisions on both sides.
+Distinct coordinate ranks provide distinct crossing identities even when several roots occur on an original cell edge.
+
+The proof is cell-relative: each supplied cell target is the restriction of the complete zero-stratum complex to its closed
+actual domain. Per-cell counts include zero vertices, edges and faces, so a cell touching a box only at a corner is certified
+as a 0D restriction and is never called zero-free. Positive-area facet incidence alone does not establish this. Global
+coverage follows only because every required root-domain rectangle is assigned to a supplied cell. The independent
+constructor does not begin with the input triangle list or assume every necessary component has a boundary trace.
+
+Every triangle edge must have two opposite uses and every indexed vertex link must be a connected cycle. These tests
+are necessary checks of the constructed indexed complex, not substitutes for the prior exhaustive zero-stratum argument.
+Rectangles of the Cartesian arrangement have disjoint relative interiors and meet only in common grid subfaces, so their
+indexed complex has the intended geometric embedding before rounding.
+
+The prepared octree tags are historical decision evidence. They are not mutated when construction succeeds. The profile
+observer retains those first decisions, records actual per-cell arrangement meshes, and emits a terminal outcome snapshot
+with resolved copies only when the indexed correspondence survives cleanup. A zero unresolved count therefore means the
+new construction completed the geometry, not that the earlier simple-cell tests passed.
+
+## Features and cleanup
+
+The complete rectangle adjacency induces the crease graph: an edge whose two incident rectangles have different oriented
+plane normals is a sharp segment. All such segments are enumerated, using the original tied owner paths on their incident
+facets. The fallback compiles these exact straight segments and planar rectangle carriers into a separate feature set.
+Existing feature-chain and quality audits then inspect that graph. A segment uses its own `[0,1]` curve interval; this
+is a complete but deliberately subdivided graph, not a minimal maximal-crease representation.
+
+Existing assembly, planar flips, surface refinement and every requested quality stage execute. Per-rectangle patch IDs
+make edits conservative. Coverage is retained only if the complete indexed lifecycle snapshot is unchanged:
+
+- All point IDs, keys and all six stored f64 payload fields.
+- Every oriented triangle and its patch owner.
+- Every mesh, protected or identified edge, including empty curve-membership sets.
+- Every curve identity and exact interval endpoint bit pattern.
+
+The existing compactor only injectively renumbers retained vertices. A changed snapshot conservatively withdraws all
+arrangement cell certificates, even if a more sophisticated proof could transport them. It does not add a mesher failure
+or trigger serial recovery. The mandatory coarse mesh incurs zero quality edits when all quality stages are requested;
+those stages and their final audits nevertheless run. Future quality improvement may need larger planar patch domains
+and a geometric common-refinement certificate rather than these deliberately restrictive rectangle identities.
+
+## Float32 embedding
+
+Every coordinate actually used by a facet must remain finite and **strictly ordered** after float32 conversion.
+A coordinate-wise, piecewise-linear increasing map taking each original cut to its rounded cut extends to an ambient
+homeomorphism of the represented domain. On each arrangement rectangle, it is affine in the two free coordinates.
+Consequently it maps the exact rectangle triangulation to the exported float32 triangulation without collapsing sheets,
+reversing triangles or creating intersections. Failure of strict order is explicit uncertainty; epsilon welding is absent.
+
+This is stronger than the earlier abstract SFCC cell certificate, but applies only to this rectilinear construction and
+only while its lifecycle snapshot survives. The displacement is bounded by the Euclidean norm of the largest coordinate
+rounding error on each axis. No numerical Hausdorff bound is currently reported by the public API. For the frozen coarse
+fixture every primitive boundary plane is exactly representable in float32, and an independent rational oracle verifies
+its exact exported surface coverage.
+
+## Real worker transport
+
+Each actual worker receives the common prepared-leaf manifest, reconstructs the bounded arrangement, and constructs only
+its owned triangle payload records for transmission. Arrangement computation is currently redundant across workers;
+this is a correctness path, not a promised parallel speedup. The `BXC1` format includes the full actual original expression
+signature, the shared leaf manifest, group identity, facet identities, and all six f64 payload fields of every triangle
+vertex. Padding fields remain literal zero.
+
+The receiver independently reconstructs the required arrangement from the original tree and validated manifest. It checks
+lattice, exact expression, all group identities, facet ownership, complete required-facet coverage, and every transported
+payload. Duplicate or missing groups/facets and changed point bits are rejected. Accepted **wire payloads** feed assembly;
+the receiver never calls the serial meshing driver. Feature identities/intervals are derived from the same independently
+verified complete rectangle adjacency. There are no transmitted success flags that can bypass geometric reconstruction.
+
+The normal prepared-partition premise remains explicit: the manifest is a product of the existing prepare/resumable
+protocol. Missing a required represented cell cannot pass because its exposed rectangles lack an owner. This is not a new
+security theorem for arbitrary hostile caller-supplied scene trees, cancellation hooks or unbounded input byte arrays.
+
+## Bounds and limitations
+
+Before large products or retained owner lists are allocated, the construction checks:
+
+- At most 1,024 expression nodes, expression depth 64, and 192 distinct coordinates per axis.
+- At most 16,384 supplied cells and 2,000,000 open strata.
+- A conservative 13 × strata × expression-nodes sign-algebra work bound of 64,000,000.
+- At most 100,000 exposed rectangles and 1,000,000 retained owner-path words.
+- At most 64,000,000 cell-containment comparisons across zero strata and emitted rectangles.
+
+The 13 factor covers nine stratum folds (one own sign and at most eight incident open-volume signs), plus four folds per
+candidate face (own sign, two side signs and one zero-owner traversal). The number of candidate arrangement faces does
+not exceed the number of open strata. Ownership traversal is postorder, not a repeated subtree rescan.
+
+There is no persistent arrangement cache or global mutable construction state. Cancellation checks occur during rank
+iteration and the existing assembly checkpoints. Bounds and unsupported arithmetic retain uncertainty; unchanged successful
+fast paths remain available. Curved primitives, blends, general transforms, nonmanifold/zero-thickness targets, large
+arrangements, arbitrary unproved quality edits and sub-float32 sheet separation are outside this construction guarantee.
