+# Candidate C results
+
+The independent C candidate constructs the frozen coarse three-sheet surface on the existing prepared leaves and default global depth. It is ready for the fourth-agent consensus review, not a claim that C has been selected or merged.
+
+| Frozen coarse case | Before | Candidate C |
+| --- | ---: | ---: |
+| Leaves | 106 | 106 |
+| Triangles | 700 | 848 |
+| Components | 1 | 2 |
+| Unresolved cells | 72 | 0 |
+| Failed cell mesher calls | 0 | 0 |
+| Legacy feature fallback cells | 9 | 0 |
+| Certified represented cells | 0 | 106 |
+
+There are 424 exact rectangles, 428 exported vertices and 152 independently identified straight crease segments. The same cube `[-128,128]^3`, padding, global depth and tolerances are retained. No output warning was removed without construction: an independent rational oracle checks all twelve target cuboid faces, orientation, area 400, signed volume 288 and pairwise interior nonoverlap. Native serial and actual WASM output both pass that oracle.
+
+The prepared leaves still carry their original exhausted-criterion tags. The constructor resolves their geometry by a different, complete local arrangement; it does not claim the former simple-cell criteria now pass. First Decision/Split events and prepare/resumable bytes remain unchanged. The profile observer records per-cell `exact-box-arrangement` meshes and a terminal outcome snapshot; certified copies are resolved there, while a changed lifecycle remains unresolved. The original tagged cells are not overwritten.
+
+## Final frozen checks
+
+- No-feature native library: **181 passed**.
+- Profile/serde configuration: **268 passed**, comprising 202 library tests and 66 integration tests: arrangement 10, coverage obstruction 6, diagnosis 11, discovery 6, cancellation 2, feature preservation 6, numerical exclusion 13, scene transforms 3 and worker partition 9.
+- All WASM fixture files, both `*_test.mts` and `*_test.mjs`: **38 passed**, no failure/skip/cancellation.
+- Native serial/resumable and actual separate WASM workers at 1/2/4/8, forward/reverse completion: identical canonical oriented eight-field vertex geometry, exact feature intervals and full validation. `serialRecovery=false` for every mandatory coarse arrangement merge.
+- Changed payload, omitted group and duplicate group transports reject. Existing sphere/cuboid snapshot and curve-membership corruption protections remain intact.
+- Independent rational oracle self-tests reject a missing face triangle, equal-area duplicated overlap and a reversed triangle.
+
+The native constructor checks enclosed boxes, disjoint interior components, a hollow wall, an annular patch, original signed nesting, reordered operands, duplicate occurrences, shared primitive planes, translation/grid phase, an actual 2:1 interface, facets exactly on shared faces, and closed-cell contacts consisting of only one vertex. Zero-only shells/edges/points, nonmanifold point contacts, float32 collapse, distinct-coordinate budget exhaustion, inconsistent grids and overlapping leaves reject. Actual WASM exports of zero-only shells/edges/points remain incomplete and carry the explicit arrangement failure reason.
+
+The existing radius-9 sphere, ordinary planar-box flip control and clipped-box seam remain on their prior paths. The fine three-sheet control retains its inherited successful mesh. The inherited quality, opaque blend, represented-rotation, lens, hidden-sphere and recovery suites pass unchanged. No new general curved-CSG guarantee is inferred from those finite regressions.
+
+The coarse rectangle mesh receives zero edits when every experimental quality operation is requested; its quality audit runs and passes. Complete indexed lifecycle snapshots detect point/key changes, rewelding, patch-owner changes, protected-edge changes, all curve intervals and empty membership sets. Changed correspondence withdraws arrangement certificates; no claim of general quality-edit proof transport is made.
+
+## Cost and bounds
+
+The mandatory coordinate product is 11 × 15 × 13 coordinate events, with 15,225 open strata. Total worker wire sizes are 131,228 / 136,952 / 148,400 / 171,296 bytes at 1/2/4/8 groups. Workers reconstruct the bounded arrangement redundantly before sending only their owned facets. The receiver reconstructs obligations and consumes the validated wire payloads; it never invokes serial mesh recovery for the successful construction.
+
+Healthy-path activation is a scan for an existing degenerate prepared leaf; it performs **zero new SDF or atomic-edge queries**. The earlier prototype rescanned atomic edges, and that trigger was removed before the frozen gates. The coordinator supplied a quiet window with other agent jobs stopped. A deliberately shortened matched run completed in16.94seconds: one process pair per scene, alternating version order across scenes, with one warmup and three timed exports per process. Median baseline→candidate times were48.440→48.568ms for the ordinary box(+0.26%),11.910→11.419ms for the clipped intersection(−4.12%), and2020.884→1998.075ms for16duplicate boxes(−1.13%). Ranges overlap; these observations do not establish a speed improvement or a precise overhead bound. Raw samples and protocol are in `timings.jsonl` and `timing-summary.json`.
+
+Per-rectangle carrier IDs deliberately restrict quality edits across rectangle borders. The exact graph is complete but subdivided, rather than a minimal maximal-crease graph. Original tied occurrence paths are retained on arrangement facets and through the full original-expression signature; generated rectangle carriers have synthetic identities.
+
+## Provenance
+
+- Frozen source logical digest: `926810ea420017340117eb1f74a842d2b4a09eb1a037d0cd966578985d5e5984`.
+- Matching focused WASM: `e94fe9ee3484a25128b230f4eb2a47982711079350eef8b07529647320449af5`, 1,572,603 bytes.
+- Native compiler: Homebrew Rust 1.99.0. WASM compiler: Rustup 1.96.0, `+simd128`. Both use release opt-level 3, LTO, one codegen unit. Node 26.11.1. All dependencies resolved offline, cargo jobs 1.
+- Matching package, native test binaries and baseline/candidate cost binaries are archived under `/tmp/sfcc-arrangement-c-final-artifacts`; exact paths and hashes are in `artifact-manifest.json`.
+- `source-manifest.json`, the frozen gate logs and independent oracle outputs accompany this report.
+
+## Failed experiments and limits
+
+The initially planned96-export cost campaign was deliberately stopped on the coordinator's instruction. At the final process inspection it had run5m55s, with the baseline256-duplicate process alone running5m38s. Its candidate counterpart never launched. The first three short-scene pairs had completed, but the original runner buffered their rows in process memory; those rows could not be recovered cleanly and no process-memory inspection was attempted. Both owned processes were terminated and their absence confirmed. The three short cases were then rerun with immediate disk recording and a45second overall limit, preserving every rerun observation. `cost-abort.json` records the unsuccessful campaign. The slow baseline process duration is neither a per-export time nor a version comparison; no favorable or unfavorable comparative256sample is inferred or discarded.
+
+
+An early precision test serialized `2^-30` through the native JSON parser and received an adjacent represented value, which was outside the exact-endpoint domain. The final precision test uses the actual exact binary value directly and establishes float32-collapse rejection. That parser difference is not counted as evidence about a different real input.
+
+An early quality test incorrectly required a nonzero edit count. The correct requirement is that requested operations execute and that changed correspondence is handled honestly. The final coarse quality control records zero edits and a completed audit. An intermediate test-only type mismatch was fixed before the final gates. Earlier passing builds are not substituted for the final source/artifact manifests.
+
+This candidate does not run the app build or browser/manual visual QA; the coordinator owns the final application gate. It does not establish a new full-workspace test count, absent external TS binary-oracle comparisons, or a general curved reconstruction/termination theorem. Scope/budget failures retain explicit uncertainty or inherited behavior as described in `proof.md`. A zero normal from the current derived vertex-normal convention is also conservatively rejected. Arbitrary unproved quality edits, sub-float32 separation, unsupported transforms and large arrangements remain outside the accepted construction.
